review_text:
Looks like a Triple A but it's not Good in every aspect but there's always something missing. Very short progression for a Live Service game—You can get to level 25 in less than 150 hours of total game (you don't even need to be the sweaty player, just be decent and understand all the mechanics which are hit the correct Stratagem code, aim in the weakspots, shoot and extract, very straight forward, it's not a issue.

By level 25 you have everything in the game available to purchase, the only thing that will require longer sessions is the samples to upgrade your S.E.S. Super Destroyer which also, is not needed, basic stuff like Donation Access License and Power Steering which is a bit more forward in the game but not that will take massive amount of time.

About the Warbonds which is the main complain of the community in how they're handled by recently adding a Warbond focused on armored vehicles with two new Exosuit which in the past and in the first game this wasn't a thing—some fancy tools weren't 'locked' behind a paywall which in my opinion is fair, complain as you want but not everything is really worth the grind except for:

- Helldivers Mobilize! Warbond: it's free so you have somewhat in between what any other warbond can offer, also includes some fancy stuff that aren't available in other warbonds (mostly cosmetic tho), again: It's free and the only free warbond so it's the main one any new player will pick;

- Democratic Demolition Warbond: if the developers don't nerf the G-123 Thermite Grenade by the time you're reading this review this is a must to choose once you pick up how to grind for Super Credits, there also some cool guns but overall the only reason is the G-123 Thermite Grenade if you're into Terminids but you can go through any other heavy target with this one;

- Control Group Warbond: by far, if not the most important warbond in my opinion, I suggest picking this one first before any other warbond just because of the LIFT-182 Warp Pack because this one will help A LOT in solo grind specially in bunkers but before buying your first warbond please remember: DO NOT PLAY THE GAME TO GRIND, PLAY TO ENJOY, I mostly played to grind and it was a mistake, quickly burnout;

- Redacted Regiment Warbond: should be the last in the priority list because this one will help a lot in Commando missions available in the Automatons front, which also was my first warbond and stealth still by the moment I'm writing this review stupidly broken (but it's a PvE game so whatever) and is the only warbond with stealth-like guns with suppressor and stuff, it's not really needed, gimmick warbond but mostly for people that like stealth, solo and or Automatons missions.

To conclude: Is this game worth? Is this game fun? Is this game good? Yes it's worth but I'll suggest a sale in my opinion (I bought Helldivers 2 during a sale), there are some constant issues in the long run that will make you very annoyed, although this game is cheaper compared to others the improvement pacing is—in my opinion very slow. Helldivers 2 is fun, but it will depend how you play the game and how you view it, if you only play to get everything—forget about it, just ignore the grind, the fancy warbonds, the community and just play the game like any other. Helldivers 2 is a good game, it's not groundbreaking in the extraction shooter/horder shooter theme but by the fact that it's purely PvE and only PvE is a positive point so you don't have to deal with CoD-like players blasting your ass with some whacky movements.
